The '''Louyang national football team''' represents [[Louyang]] in men's international association football. It is governed by the [[Louyang Football Association]] and is one of the more established sides in the [[AFA Men's World Ranking]], where it sits 15th in June 2026. The team is closely identified with [[Louyang Capital Stadium]] and, unusually, its squad is made up of players from the capital city's club, [[Louyang City FC]], and Louyang footballers based abroad; no other domestic clubs are represented.

That structure has made Louyang one of the most centralised national teams in the AFA region. Rather than relying on a wide domestic league, the national side is built around the capital club's core and an expatriate contingent playing in foreign leagues.

== History ==

=== Early development ===
Football in Louyang developed around the capital's schools, civic clubs, and industrial associations. The sport first took root in the capital and spread outward, but it never became broadly decentralised in the way it did in some larger AFA countries.

As a result, [[Louyang City FC]] became the defining institution of Louyang football. Its players, coaches, and youth system provided the backbone of the national side, while the best prospects who left the domestic game generally moved directly into foreign clubs rather than into a deep national league.

=== Modern era ===
By the modern era, Louyang had become a compact but competitive side, known for organisation and continuity. The national team entered the [[2026 AFA World Cup]] in Group L alongside [[Aetolia national football team|Aetolia]] and [[Louyan national football team|Louyan]], marking one of the country's biggest sporting stages.

Louyang's international profile has been shaped by the contrast between its capital-heavy domestic structure and its overseas players, who bring experience from a variety of foreign tactical systems.

== Stadium ==

Louyang play their home matches at [[Louyang Capital Stadium]] in [[Louyang]], the country's principal football venue and the symbolic centre of the national game. Important matches are also occasionally staged at the Louyang City FC ground when demand or scheduling requires it.

== Playing style ==

The Louyang national team is generally described as a compact, technically tidy side that plays with strong collective understanding. The team tends to favour:

* controlled possession
* short passing through midfield
* quick transitions from the capital-club core
* disciplined defensive shape
* efficient use of set pieces

Because so many of the regulars come from the same club system, Louyang are often more cohesive than teams of similar ranking. The overseas players add pace and variety, but the side remains defined by the capital club's style and habits.

